I've been playing around more with Structured Prompting lately, focusing on Markdowns. 

Investing the time, thinking about the prompt and structuring it in a 'Markdown' format - rather than being so conversational focused (via GPT/Gemini), saves tokens, energy + forces you to learn! 

Use this guide going forward to support you.

The task spec (This is for hyper detail for reusable prompting) 
● Goal. The result you need, and why
● Audience. Who uses the output and what they do next
● Context. Additional background information needed every run
● Inputs. The materials to work from
● Process. Steps to follow, when order or a check matters
● Output. Format, length, sections and tone
● Examples. A few relevant, varied, high quality samples 
● Constraints. Rules to follow, including what to do when information is missing.
● Success criteria. How to judge the results before anyone uses it

If you are in a little more of a hurry to get something produced, use this task spec as a minimum
● Goal. The result you need, and why
● Inputs. The materials to work from
● Output. Format, length, sections and tone

